Applying the same backward compatibility check here for older `xgrammar` versions ensures robustness regardless of which branch is taken.

```suggestion
        import inspect
        if "backend" in inspect.signature(xgr.apply_token_bitmask_inplace).parameters:
            xgr.apply_token_bitmask_inplace(
                logits, grammar_bitmask, indices=index_tensor, backend=bitmask_backend
            )
        else:
            if bitmask_backend != "auto":
                logger.warning(
                    "The installed version of xgrammar does not support the 'backend' "
                    "parameter. The 'bitmask_backend' setting will be ignored."
                )
            xgr.apply_token_bitmask_inplace(logits, grammar_bitmask, indices=index_tensor)
```

